    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0652" n="552" xml:id="pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-15T09:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1920—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>199. Copies Tokyo, Peking. Department’s telegram June 11, 1 p.m.<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d636-f1"/> Vladivostok provisional government recognizes Far Eastern
                    Republic at Verkhneudinsk and their relations are good. Both announce desire for
                    union as soon as Semenoff barrier removed but no mention so far of terms on
                    which this could be effected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
